    "body": "2026 SEMA Show • Mitsubishi Returns to Las Vegas With the Fresh 2028 Outlander Diamond Trail Edition\nNew Hot Wheels Elite 64 Mercedes-AMG ONE Is Just Around the Corner\n12 photos\nPhoto: Mattel Creations\nI am sometimes shocked at how quickly Mattel will come out with a 1/64th-scale version of a car that just debuted on the international stage. It can take up to a year in some cases, and I guess it all depends on the deals that go on behind the scenes. It’s not always smooth sailing, though.\nTake for instance the Ferrari situation. The diecast manufacturer had lost the license over a decade ago, and Hot Wheels fans had no other choice but to get their tiny prancing ponies from other companies. That problem is being dealt with right now, ever since Mattel and Ferrari signed a new agreement circa 2024.\nI know the Heritage Set showed up as a Red Line Club special release in 2025, but think of the development process and time needed to get that result. Anyway, I’m not here to talk about Hot Wheels Ferraris, as Mercedes-AMG is the star of the show here. Seeing this brand-new casting reminds me I just missed purchasing the '89 Mercedes-Benz 560 SEC AMG from my local dealer.\nAnd something tells me that its first-ever Premium variation is just as desirable as the Elite 64 collectible in today’s story. And that also brings me back to what I was saying earlier: this car has been around since 2022! We’ve had to wait four years for a Hot Wheels version of it, and I can think of a few reasons why it hasn’t happened so far.\nThe licensing costs might have been too high for the deal to make sense, or maybe the team in El Segundo just didn’t know which series this casting would best fit in. Elite 64 launched in 2023, but it was a rather slow start with only six items in one year. Anyway, it’s just around the corner now, and I must say I am slightly disappointed it doesn’t feature the opening gullwing doors like the real thing.\nI realize that could have placed it in RLC-exclusive territory, where it would have wound up costing $35 or more. Resellers in my area are already asking a bit more than that as they’re taking advantage of the shipping restrictions, so there’s that. The AMG One is the third Mercedes collectible in Elite 64 this year, after the 300 SL and the G 63 AMG 6×6.\nI pre-ordered the latter a while ago and I’m not sure what happened to it. We all know the AMG One won’t be nearly as desirable as the upcoming hauler that several creators have been teasing recently. That one is bound to sell out within the first 60 seconds, while the Mercedes hypercar might even become a virtual peg-warmer (at least for a few weeks).\nI’m not convinced this series will survive beyond 2027, but I also don’t have any sort of access to any numbers on how it’s going. I don’t plan on buying this collectible, but you can give it a try on the 29th of October , 2026 at 9 AM PT. I have to admit the presentation photos are pretty cool, though!\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nHot Wheels Elite 64 Mercedes-Benz Mercedes-AMG One Mattel Creations\nAbout the author: Dragos Chitulescu\nThe things Dragos enjoys the most in life are, in no particular order: cars, motorcycles, diecast cars, and drifting. He's seen (and driven) many vehicles since he started his writing career back in 2009, but his garage currently houses a 1991 Mazda RX-7 FC3S Turbo II and a 1999 Suzuki SV650-S. Full profile\nUP NEXT Billionaire Lord’s Prestigious Italian Superyacht Is Asking for $27M",
